"""Draft PR for the sandbox milestone; close #109-#114."""
import os, subprocess, re, time
from github import Github

token = os.environ.get("GH_TOKEN") or os.environ.get("TOKEN")
full = re.search(r"[:/]([^/]+/[^/]+?)(?:\.git)?$",
                 subprocess.check_output(["git", "remote", "get-url", "origin"], text=True).strip()).group(1)
repo = Github(token).get_repo(full)

def retry(fn, *a, **k):
    for i in range(5):
        try:
            return fn(*a, **k)
        except Exception as e:
            if i == 4: raise
            print(f"  transient ({type(e).__name__}), retry..."); time.sleep(3 + i * 2)

BODY = """## Summary
Milestone #13 — a sandbox mode where the player builds maps from the
game's own pieces, places NPCs from BOTH character pools, saves them as
human-readable JSON, and plays them with dialogue fully working. Zero
new runtime systems: placed pieces compile to normal `Building` rows, so
collision (City) and rendering (Assets) are the existing paths. One
atomic commit per issue.

**#109 data contract** (`4d1dd03`) — 20-piece catalog (one data row per
piece), version-gated map JSON (strict integer tiles: off-grid is
impossible by construction; byte-stable round-trip), `validateMap`
returning EVERY problem with retry-feedback-quality messages (the LLM
world-gen plan reuses them verbatim), and `buildCity` via a new
`City::fromBuildings` factory. Sandbox cities carry `hasStreets()=false`.

**#110 repopulation seam** (`b4149dc`) — `World::loadCity` swaps
contents in place (World can't be reassigned; the world bus deliberately
survives); main's town spawning extracts into `spawnTownRoster` /
`resetNpcSideArrays`. Town↔sandbox↔town round-trip pinned by test.

**#111 asset identity** (`ce6230a`) — instance-suffixed ids
(`bakery#2`) resolve base assets everywhere (model, size spec, and the
fountain composite dispatch — the last one caught by a fixture
screenshot rendering the fountain as a hashed generic building);
`--map <file>` boots a fixture headlessly; renderer skips the authored
downtown road/slab pass for sandbox cities.

**#112 editor** (`4d787eb`) — tilted pan/zoom camera, mouse unprojected
to the grid with a ghost of the current piece drawn through the NORMAL
building paths (green/red by live validator verdict), click place /
right-click delete / [ ] cycle, P to play (spawning at the first clear
spot), Escape saves + restores the town. Menu gains a Sandbox page
(logged v1 cut: New auto-names maps `map-N`; no name text field).

**#113 NPC placement** (`4125982`) — `resolvePlacedNpc` (core, tested)
is the one spawn door: `persona:<stem>` from the roster,
`character:<id>` from the store, placement position/facing, schedules
CLEARED (town coordinates are nonsense in custom maps — logged). Tab
switches piece/NPC placement; ghosts are the character's real look.

**#114 QA gate** (`fb3e0db`) — `--map` also spawns placed NPCs;
visual-qa subagent verdict on the fixture village: **PASS** (real
models at downtown-consistent scale, composite fountain, both placed
NPCs matched to their authored looks, correct human-vs-doorway
